332-///
333-/// Every nested bracket, prefix operator, call argument and left-associative
334-/// binary chain makes the expression tree one level deeper. Parsing recurses
335-/// per level and dropping the finished tree recurses per level, so an
336-/// unbounded depth turns a long line of source into "has overflowed its stack"
337-/// and a core dump instead of a diagnostic.
338-///
339-/// The value is deliberately small. libstd gives a spawned thread a 2 MiB
340-/// stack, and a debug build spends roughly 16 KiB of stack per level of nested
341-/// brackets (eleven frames of `parse_primary` .. `parse_postfix`). Measured on
342-/// this repository, 123 levels is where a 2 MiB test thread dies; 64 leaves
343-/// nearly a 2x margin while staying far above anything hand-written.
